[
  {
    "title": "Critical to the operation of the blockchain",
    "description": "Security-relevant parameters from the network and economic groups. A change needs the DReps, the SPOs and the Constitutional Committee.",
    "parameterDetails": "## Critical to the operation of the blockchain\n### Network group\n- **Maximum block body size** (maxBlockBodySize): Defines the maximum size of a block's body in bytes\n- **Maximum transaction size** (maxTxSize): The maximum allowed size for a transaction\n- **Maximum block header size** (maxBlockHeaderSize): The maximum allowed size for a block header\n- **Maximum size of a serialized asset value** (maxValueSize): Maximum byte size of serialized values\n- **Maximum script execution units in a single block** (maxBlockExecutionUnits[steps/memory]): Limits script execution per block\n\n### Economic group\n- **Minimum fee coefficient** (txFeePerByte): The fee charged per byte of a transaction\n- **Minimum fee constant** (txFeeFixed): The fixed minimum fee for a transaction\n- **Minimum fee per byte for reference scripts** (minFeeRefScriptCoinsPerByte): Fee for reference script bytes\n- **Minimum lovelace deposit per byte of serialized UTxO** (utxoCostPerByte): Cost of UTxO storage\n\nA change needs at least 67% of the active DRep voting stake, at least 51% of the active SPO voting stake and two thirds of the Constitutional Committee. At least 90 days should normally pass between the off-chain proposal and the on-chain governance action.",
